R-SP6 R-SP7 R-UP1 R-UP3 R-UP5 R-UP8 R-UP10 R-UP11 R-CM5 R-VA5 R-SP25 R-C8 R-C9 R-C6 R-WS1 R-OUT4 R-J3 (slice 038, `tln upgrade` for packages): 13 runs on 11 projects and one workspace. The command code is `Upgrade.run!`, `Vars.scope` (arm `Upgrade`), `Ranges.rewrite`, `Lags.rewrites`.
The world: pfx 0.1.0 to 0.2.1 (platform), json 2.0.0 to 3.1.0 (3.1.0 is young, so it is hidden, R-C6), parser 1.0.0, 1.2.0, 2.0.0 (2.0.0 names json 2.1.0).
Run 1 (p1, no `talon.toml`): all variables are free, with no range. json goes to the series 3, parser and pf to a new series. Each moved line ends with `new series`. The header of parser 2.0.0 keeps json 2.1.0 in the closure: the warning R-C8 on stderr (R-UP3). No file is created (R-UP5).
Run 2 (p2, `talon.toml` with a comment, an unknown key `lex`, an anchor `parser = "=1.0.0"`): the anchor is held and Talon prints `parser: anchor, held` (R-UP1). json and pf move, and their keys get `^3.0` and `0.2.*`. The comment, the order and `lex` stay (R-UP5).
Run 3 (p3, `upgrade parser`): a named anchor is free (R-VA5). It moves to 2.0.0 and the key becomes `=2.0.0` (R-UP5).
Run 4 (p4, `upgrade json`, key `json = "acme/json@^2.1"`): only json is free. The key keeps its `acme/json@` form: `acme/json@^3.0`. pf and parser are held (R-SP7).
Run 5 (`--strategy lowest`): exit 2 (R-UP8). No file call is made after the options.
Run 6 (workspace, member a, key `json = "^2.1"` in the root file): both members move. The root key `json` is rewritten once (R-SP25). Member b has the same group as `j2` and there is no key for it: Talon adds no key (R-UP5).
Run 7 (p7, `update`): the old rule. A range `^2.1` and `0.1.*` hold the variables: json 2.2.0, pf 0.1.1, `talon.toml` does not change (R-UP10).
Run 8 (p5, `update json@latest`, key `^2.1`): the newest release in the series 3, and the key becomes `^3.0` (R-UP11, R-SL5).
Run 9 (p6, `update json@latest`, no `talon.toml`): the same move, and no file is created (R-UP5).
Run 10 (p8, `upgrade --dry-run --json`): the envelope has `"command":"upgrade"` and the fields `moved` and `toml`. Nothing is written (R-J3).
Run 11 (p9, `upgrade json`, key `json = ">=2.1, <3.0"`): the range has no form of R-UP5 and does not admit 3.0.2. The key stays, and the note `talon.toml: json: the range does not admit 3.0.2, change it by hand` is printed (Q1 (b), review 2026-10-24). No toml line.
Run 12 (p10, `upgrade json`, `[resolution] strategy = "lowest"` and key `^2.1`): `upgrade` ignores the key of the file and uses the highest release (Q2 (a)). The key becomes `^3.0`, and the toml line ends with `(was "^2.1")` (Q6 (a)).
Run 13 (p11, `update json@^2.1 parser@^1`, keys `json = "^2.1"` and `parser = "=1.0.0"`): the key of json gets the value that it has already, the key of parser changes, so the file is written. The line of json has no `(was ...)`, the line of parser ends with `(was "=1.0.0")` (gap A10 of the code agent, Q6).
